<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices inch down at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices inch down at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>All minimum prices of Polish T-bills fell by one grosz at today's primary auction on total demand of 836 million zlotys against a 1.2 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 656 million zlotys worth of the bills.</p>
<p>			 8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     95.48    91.13     --	83.50</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.49)  (91.14)    --     (83.51)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.55    91.17     --	83.80</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.54)  (91.17)    --     (83.83)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     300.0    200.0     --	700.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --	86.8    243.8     --	505.1</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --	73.8    242.8     --	339.4</p>
<p>   next auction	--     250.0    250.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>   pvs announced offer     (200.0)  (200.0)    --     (300.0)</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys. The treasury raised the offer for the next auction -- previously announced offer size in brackets below the revised values.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
